
<div>
    <div class="form-group">
        <div>
            <p>Pfam and InterPro databases define domain boundaries for members of their families.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mb-3">
            <div>
                <span class="input-heading">Domain:</span>
                <span>
                    {{ form_widget(form.domain) }}
                </span>
            </div>
            <div class="submission-error">{{ form_errors(form.domain) }}</div>
            {% if form.domainFamily is defined %}
                <div>
                    <span class="input-heading">Family:</span>
                    {{ form_widget(form.domainFamily) }}
                    <label for="{{ form.domainFamily.vars.id }}" class="form-label">Use domain boundaries from the specified family (enter only one family).</label>
                </div>
                <div class="submission-error">{{ form_errors(form.domainFamily) }}</div>
            {% endif %}
            <div>
                <span class="input-heading">Region:</span>
				<div class="radio-group-wrapper">
                    {% for child in form.domainRegion %}
                        <span class="radio-item-inline">
                            {{ form_widget(child) }}
                            {{ form_label(child) }}
                        </span>
                    {% endfor %}
                </div>
                <div class="submission-error">{{ form_errors(form.domainRegion) }}</div>
            </div>
            <div class="input-description">
                If enabled, only the sequence corresponding to the defined domain for the family(ies) will be used for the computation.
                If the N-terminal option is selected, the sequence that is N-terminal to the specified domain will be used.
                If the C-terminal option is selected, the sequence that is C-terminal to the specified domain will be used.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

